 util-linux,
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends}
Replaces:
 uperf-linux-gui
Description: capability-driven userspace performance scheduler
 A Rust daemon and command-line tools for coordinating Linux ARM64 CPU,
 GPU and workload performance policy.
 .
 The service is deliberately left disabled and stopped after installation.
 The administrator must review and validate the device configuration before
 enabling it.

Package: uperf-linux-gui
Section: utils
Architecture: arm64
Conflicts:
 uperf-linux
Depends:
 dbus,
 polkitd | policykit-1,
 systemd,
 util-linux,
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends}
Replaces:
 uperf-linux
Description: capability-driven userspace performance scheduler with GUI
 A complete graphical edition containing the uperf-linux daemon, command-line
 tools, read-only probe, system integration, and a GTK4/libadwaita client.
 Targets, operating points, modes and telemetry are populated from daemon
 capabilities rather than from device-specific constants.
 .
 This package is an alternative to the headless uperf-linux package; the two
 editions cannot be installed at the same time.
